cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this verification package, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Verification package for openai/math family 003, Uniform exclusion of Landau–Siegel zeros: machine-checked complement to existing human write-ups (comparator + nanoda, Lean Lemma 3, explicit constant)"
abstract: "A machine-checked complement to existing human write-ups of the OpenAI argument for the uniform exclusion of Landau–Siegel zeros (OpenAI, manuscript dated October 1, 2026; openai/math family 003): W. D. Banks, arXiv:2610.15483; B. Kerr, arXiv:2610.21099; B. Green, Hexagon 2610.00311v2. The package records what can be checked by machine: acceptance of the Lean formalization by the official comparator with two kernels (Lean and nanoda) (IP and Unix-domain sockets blocked by a seccomp filter; see the 2026-10-26 network note); a Lean proof of the paper's Lemma 3 (a step of OpenAI's and Banks's route); the challenge theorem rerouted through it; an Arb-certified explicit constant, conditional on the paper's proof, compared term by term with Banks's; and exact small-N checks. Not refereed; not a proof of the theorem."
authors:
